{"id":"chatcmpl-d8a785b3-5db8-4155-b429-e47f28d52d49","object":"chat.completion","created":1795245008,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a cross-validation strategy for medical image interpretation: when a visual finding must be localized to a specific side, query multiple independent vision-language models with anatomically explicit prompts and require agreement before committing to an answer. The key abstraction is using redundant expert tools to resolve spatial/laterality ambiguity rather than trusting a single model's output.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a task requires determining spatial laterality (left/right, above/below) from ambiguous imaging, query multiple independent expert models and require convergent localization before answering.\",\n    \"Frame tool prompts with explicit anatomical reference landmarks (e.g., 'relative to spine and heart', 'patient left or right based on anatomical landmarks') to force models to reason about orientation rather than guess.\",\n    \"Use a second model as an independent cross-validator specifically when the first model's output could be confounded by view orientation (e.g., lateral views where left/right is non-obvious).\",\n    \"Commit to an answer only after multiple independent sources agree on the same localization; treat single-source localization as insufficient for spatially ambiguous findings.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging interpretation\": \"For laterality or localization questions, prompt models with explicit anatomical landmarks and cross-check with a second independent model before answering.\",\n    \"Ambiguous spatial reasoning tasks\": \"When orientation is non-obvious (mirrored, rotated, or lateral views), require redundant independent confirmations rather than trusting one model's spatial judgment.\",\n    \"Multi-tool verification workflows\": \"Design prompts so each tool independently reasons about the same spatial question; agreement across tools is the signal to answer, disagreement warrants further probing.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm each tool prompt explicitly asks for laterality using anatomical landmarks (not just 'where is it').\",\n    \"Verify at least two independent tools converge on the same side before selecting the answer option.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":447,"total_tokens":846,"completion_tokens":399,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":447},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":399}}}